  <h2>Reinforcement: Corner Protectors vs. Stretch Film</h2>
  <p>
    When you compress clothes, the box becomes the primary defense.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stretch Film:</strong> Essential. It prevents the vacuum seal from failing if the outer box gets damp in transit. Without film, a small puncture can cause your jacket to "re-inflate," potentially bursting the box.</li>
    <li><strong>Corner Protectors:</strong> Essential for heavy hauls, but skip them for "Clothing Only" parcels to keep the outer dimensions as small as possible.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timing your Winter Haul: Avoid the "Puffer Peaks"</h2>
  <p>
    Don't wait until December. Logistics hubs in Guangzhou and Hong Kong experience massive "Puffer Peaks" in late November. Shipping your winter finds in <strong>September or October</strong> can save you 15% in seasonal surcharges and avoid the 10-day backlogs common in winter.
  </p>

